e pressure on the Landlord, preventing them from playing low singles freely, which helps my teammate.\n\nReason: This move attempts a "checkmate" or forces a high-value response (Bomb/222) from the Landlord. Playing singles would surrender tempo to the Landlord, who likely holds Jokers and 2s, making it hard for me to clear my low cards later. Keeping the 8 is slightly better than keeping the 6 as it can beat a few more low cards (3-7) if the opportunity arises.\n\nAnswer: {"cards": ["♠6", "♠A", "♥A", "♦A"]}'}
